        'grammar-a1-1' => ['skill' => 'grammar', 'level' => 'A1', 'title' => 'Present Simple: Daily Routines',
            'content' => "## What you\'ll learn\nThe present simple is one of the most important tenses in English. You use it to talk about things that happen regularly \u2014 your daily routine, habits, and general facts. After this lesson, you will be able to describe what you do every day with correct verb forms.\n\n## How it works\nThe present simple uses the base form of the verb for I, you, we, and they. For he, she, and it, you add -s to the end of the verb. Negatives use do not (don\'t) or does not (doesn\'t) plus the base form. Questions use Do/Does at the start.\n> I wake up at seven o\'clock every morning.\n\n## Common mistakes at this level\n- \"She go to school every day.\" \u2192 \"She goes to school every day.\" (Remember -s for he/she/it.)\n- \"I doesn\'t like coffee.\" \u2192 \"I don\'t like coffee.\" (Use don\'t with I/you/we/they.)\n\n## Try it yourself\nWrite three sentences about your morning routine using the present simple. Use time expressions like \"every day\" or \"always\" to make your sentences more natural.",
